From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:40:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] B70: a different research request starts a new session

Travel and product sessions latch their capability for the life of the
session. A different research request sent into one was refused ("send
/new"). A queued product question after a travel run was withheld
(2026-10-08 Tucson).

- Idle message: before the session is claimed, a research request whose route
  differs from the session's latched travel or product route is moved to a
  fresh session. A new product request in a product session counts too. The
  move uses the /new handler, and the chat gets "Started a new session ...
  /resume <previous id>". Approvals, "more" and other continuations stay.
  Ordinary messages return synchronously, so the session claim still happens
  before the handler first yields.
- Queued message: a queued follow-up that is such a request is not run in the
  finishing session. It is re-dispatched through the adapter once the run
  releases, and the idle path then moves it to a new session.
- The busy acknowledgement says a different request will start in a new
  session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
